{
  "original_id": "primary-20260914-bigdescent-logconcavity",
  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260914-bigdescent_logconcavity",
  "title": "Conditional Schur positivity for binary-word events with at most four free positions",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every n>=1, let a_n(A) count binary words of length n ending in 1 whose event set A consists exactly of the ending positions of factors 10 and 011. For every J subset of {2,...,n} with m=|J|<=4 and every S subset of {2,...,n}\\J, the homogeneous symmetric polynomial H_(S,J)(x,y)=sum_(T subset J) a_n(S union T) a_n(S union (J\\T)) x^|T| y^(m-|T|) is Schur-positive in two variables. Thus, if G(t;z)=sum_(T subset J) a_n(S union T)t^|T| product_(i in T) z_i=sum_k g_k(z)t^k, every g_k(z)^2-g_(k-1)(z)g_(k+1)(z) is coefficientwise nonnegative, with g_k=0 outside its range. There is no bound on n, the spacing of J, or |S|; all other event indicators are fixed, and zero-count cases are included. The two-position inequality a_n(S)a_n(S union {i,j})<=2a_n(S union {i})a_n(S union {j}) has optimal factor 2, attained at n=4,S=empty,{i,j}={2,4}. The pair-polynomial conclusion also holds for arbitrary |J| when J can be partitioned in its natural order into blocks of at most four positions such that, between each consecutive pair of blocks, S contains two adjacent positions. No unrestricted weighted theorem, full exceptional-class log-concavity, or resolution of the original 21-family assertion is claimed.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
